Dispatch GTK repaint requests on the UI thread.

Window::RequestPaint explicitly permits non-UI callers. The GTK backend
called gtk_widget_queue_draw directly from the GPU command thread, violating
GTK's threading contract. Three aka core dumps crashed in g_slist_find via
GDK invalidation from Presenter::RefreshGuestOutput; a live debugger caught
the same worker-thread call on its first breakpoint hit.

Use the same mutex-protected gdk_threads_add_idle dispatch as the existing
GTKWindowedAppContext. Coalesce requests and cancel the source after surface
disconnection, on both close and destruction, before its owner disappears.
No synchronous call into the UI loop: the caller may hold paint_mode_mutex_.
Windows and SDL backends are unchanged.

The real GTKWindow regression test is tests/gtk-repaint.cpp in this flake.
It checks UI-thread ownership, coalescing, close/reopen and pending destruction.

